# Fork: findings the secret scan (.github/scripts/fork-secret-scan.sh) may skip, by fingerprint.
# Keep it empty: allow a reviewed fake key with an exact-value entry in .gitleaks.toml instead (the
# rule, the file and the value; see "A reviewed fake key" there), or a `gitleaks:allow` comment on
# the line itself where the file allows one.
#
# Why not here: a fingerprint names a line number, not a value.
#   file:rule:line (no commit) hides every key of that rule on that line, in every commit, including
#   a real key a later commit puts there. The scan refuses such lines (the job fails).
#   commit:file:rule:line matches only that commit, but a squash merge gives the commit a new id, so
#   the default branch's push scan fails on the same finding; the scan warns about such lines.
#
# The scan reads this file from the default branch (a pull request) or the tip before the push, so a
# change here applies once it is merged: land it in a pull request of its own first.
